1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:18,140
Let's move on to the next chapter. We said interrupts fall into three categories: external interrupts, software interrupts, and timer interrupts. Timer interrupts are also very important, so we have a separate chapter to introduce them.

2
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:23,630
So, as for timer interrupts,

3
00:00:23,630 --> 00:00:26,070
I'll introduce them to you in these three parts.

4
00:00:26,070 --> 00:00:27,870
First, let's look at what a timer interrupt is.

5
00:00:27,870 --> 00:00:30,670
Now, as mentioned earlier,

6
00:00:30,670 --> 00:00:32,250
the timer interrupt is a type of interrupt.

7
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:32,490
Right?

8
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:33,970
And it belongs to a type called local interrupts.

9
00:00:33,970 --> 00:00:37,950
That much is straightforward.

10
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:41,670
So why do we call it a local interrupt?

11
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:44,570
Basically, it's because it isn't triggered by a peripheral.

12
00:00:44,570 --> 00:00:48,230
It isn't triggered by those ordinary external devices.

13
00:00:48,230 --> 00:00:49,630
Rather, there is a dedicated

14
00:00:49,630 --> 00:00:54,070
component inside our chip,

15
00:00:54,070 --> 00:00:59,890
a special device called the CLINT,

16
00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:02,650
a device built into the SoC chip,

17
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:04,030
and it is this device that raises the interrupt.

18
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:08,190
It's called the Core Local Interruptor,

19
00:01:08,190 --> 00:01:09,250
which is what the abbreviation stands for.

20
00:01:09,250 --> 00:01:13,470
CLINT is short for Core Local Interruptor.

21
00:01:13,470 --> 00:01:15,090
So this thing,

22
00:01:15,090 --> 00:01:19,610
it comes with our chip specifically

23
00:01:19,610 --> 00:01:21,130
as a device attached to it.

24
00:01:21,130 --> 00:01:23,250
As for this device,

25
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:27,470
it is responsible for generating two kinds of interrupts:

26
00:01:27,470 --> 00:01:29,770
one kind is called software interrupt,

27
00:01:29,770 --> 00:01:30,870
and the other is called timer interrupt.

28
00:01:30,870 --> 00:01:34,730
We can see the blue line and the red line in the diagram.

29
00:01:34,730 --> 00:01:40,410
Now let's focus mainly on its timer interrupt.

30
00:01:40,410 --> 00:01:45,670
Now, for this device, we do the same thing.

